From: libwebsockets upstream
Subject: [PATCH] ws: preserve inflater draining state before client callbacks

回移上游 f41c8e66b0989c60c22af68d294cea9509b7f9fa 中的库修复，
不包含该提交的示例程序改动。v5.0-stable 回移提交为
989bfca485bd57320dfc46a8c90a532759179879。

上游问题：https://github.com/warmcat/libwebsockets/issues/3660
上游提交：https://github.com/warmcat/libwebsockets/commit/f41c8e66b0989c60c22af68d294cea9509b7f9fa

--- a/lib/roles/ws/client-parser-ws.c
+++ b/lib/roles/ws/client-parser-ws.c
@@ -59,6 +59,17 @@ _lws_ws_client_rx_payload_passthrough(struct lws *wsi, const uint8_t *buf,
 		}
 		if (n == PMDR_DID_NOTHING)
 			break;
+
+		/*
+		 * We want the user callback done with the draining state set
+		 * if the extension still has pending output, because
+		 * lws_is_final_fragment() hides that it was final until the
+		 * last chunk of the inflated message has been delivered
+		 */
+		if (n == PMDR_HAS_PENDING)
+			lws_add_wsi_to_draining_ext_list(wsi);
+		else
+			lws_remove_wsi_from_draining_ext_list(wsi);
 #endif
 
 		if (wsi->ws->check_utf8 && !wsi->ws->defeat_check_utf8) {
